    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d800">

                <pb facs="1268" n="1254" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 European War/10–1044</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by Mr. E. Tomlin Bailey of the Special War
                        Problems Division</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1944-10-10">October 10, 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Gunningham<anchor n="43" xml:id="d800-f1"/> telephoned to say that he had
                    been informed by the Foreign Office that they did not think it necessary that
                    the British and American protests concerning the German mistreatment of
                    parachutists had to be identical. The Foreign Office is forwarding copies of the
                    correspondence and statements made during the discussions with Germany after the
                    fall of Crete and Mr. Gunningham promised to send copies of these documents to
                    the Department for its information as well as a copy of the British note which
                    is shortly to be sent.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d800-f2"/>
                </p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d800-f1" n="43" xml:id="d800-f1-content">
                <p>H. W. Gunningham, Second Secretary of the British Embassy at Washington.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d800-f2" n="44" xml:id="d800-f2-content">
                <p>Mr. Gunningham transmitted copies of the 1940 correspondence in his note of
                    October 20, 1944; none printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
